                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "34063472",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198048479010",
                            "num_reviews": 24,
                            "playtime_forever": 248,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 248,
                            "last_played": 1502034211
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I laughed quite a bit during this game; the game was well worth the $4.00 price.  \n\nThis visual novel is a parody of the 1970s' James Bond movies, sort of what you would get if Goldfinger and Dr. Horrible's Sing-Along Blog got together and had a love child.  The main character is an archvillain's protege who is trying to make it into the big League--the League of Villains.  It's a M/M visual novel with two love interests.\n\n:: Pros ::\nCute story.\nAttractive character design.  The characters look like adults.\nNifty soundtrack - I actually paused on pages to listen to the complete loops.\nFunny bits involving Henchmen whose names you can never remember and sharks. \n\n:: Cons ::\nStory is too short. All achievements can be gained in under 4 hours, if you use skip function.\nYou can't name the character or his alias.\nOnly five or six uncomplicated choices on each story path.\nTypos. \n\nI wouldn't mind seeing more games from this developer, preferably with more sharks.  \n\n\n\n",
